DATA

Exercise catalogue: web/public/catalog/exercises.json
  Source:  free-exercise-db, by Yuhonas and contributors
           https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db
           commit f00c92c7dcf1216a928a52c3706c7ce8e2f71ed5
  Licence: The Unlicense (public domain)
  Built by tools/exercises/fetch_exercises.py. The exercise photos are not stored here: the app
  loads them from the same commit of that repository.

Food composition data: web/public/catalog/crea_foods.csv, and the food names in
tools/food-model/classes.csv
  Source:  CREA, Centro di ricerca Alimenti e Nutrizione,
           "Tabelle di composizione degli alimenti"
           https://www.alimentinutrizione.it/sezioni/tabelle-nutrizionali
  Terms:   free to reuse, provided the source is cited as above.
  Built by tools/crea/extract_crea.py.

Packaged food products
  Source:  Open Food Facts, https://world.openfoodfacts.org
  Licence: Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0
  Nothing from Open Food Facts is stored in this repository: the app queries it from the user's
  browser when they search for a product or scan a barcode.


PHOTO FOOD RECOGNISER: web/public/models/food-recognizer.onnx, web/public/models/food-classes.json

Backbone
  DINOv2 ViT-S/14 ("facebook/dinov2-small"), by Meta Platforms, Inc.
  https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov2
  Licence: Apache License 2.0, text in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt
  Changes: the backbone is used unchanged. Two single-layer heads were added and trained on top of
  it, and the whole model was exported to ONNX (see tools/food-model).

The heads were trained on:
  - MyFoodRepo / AIcrowd Food Recognition Benchmark 2022 (AIcrowd and EPFL): CC BY 4.0
  - Nutrition5k (Google Research): CC BY 4.0
  - Open Images V7 (Google): labels CC BY 4.0, photos CC BY 2.0
  - COCO 2017: annotations CC BY 4.0; only photos licensed CC BY, with no known copyright
    restriction, or US Government works
  Licence texts: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ and
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/

The model runs in the browser with ONNX Runtime Web (Microsoft, MIT License).


SOFTWARE LIBRARIES

The app is built with open-source libraries, listed in web/package.json and, with their exact
versions, in web/package-lock.json. Among them: React, React Router, Zod, zod-to-json-schema,
Dexie, PowerSync with wa-sqlite, Supabase Auth, ONNX Runtime Web, ZXing and qrcode.

